    docs(driver): link the Agent Driver guide from README and GETTING-STARTED and correct the @kind/fence rule (UX-005 judge fix)
    
    Judge verdict 836c944f failed one criterion: the guide had zero inbound links,
    so the audience it names (an agent session told to use SpecLang) could not find
    it. Added to README's Documentation list and the GETTING-STARTED "For AI Agents"
    ladder.
    
    Also corrected a documented claim after probing it: section 5 said non-code
    kinds are skipped, but a fenced @kind:endpoint block emits a file (measured:
    "Generated: 1 files", ping.ts 201 bytes, with a tagged fence; "Generated: 0
    files" with an untagged fence). The fence decides, not the @kind.
    
    Addresses UX-005.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
